      "side": 1,
      "message": "In my experience, most i2c devices work like this:\n\nRead register:\n  S \u003ci2c_addr|W\u003e \u003creg_addr\u003e R \u003ci2c_addr|R\u003e \u003cdata0\u003e .. \u003cdataN\u003e P\n\nWrite register:\n  S \u003ci2c_addr|W\u003e \u003creg_addr\u003e \u003cdata0\u003e .. \u003cdataN\u003e P\n\nSo, I think you are you saying for TPM *read* transactions, we must do this instead:\n\nRead TPM register:\n  S \u003ci2c_addr|W\u003e \u003creg_addr\u003e P  I  S \u003ci2c_addr|R\u003e \u003cdata0\u003e .. \u003cdataN\u003e P\n\nBut write-tpm-register transactions are as still similar to the above:\nWrite TPM register:\n  S \u003ci2c_addr|W\u003e \u003creg_addr\u003e \u003cdata0\u003e .. \u003cdataN\u003e P  I\n\nwhere:\n  S: i2c Start\n  R: i2c Repeated-start\n  P: i2c Stop\n  I: GPIO_INT_AP_L (Cr50-\u003eAP interrupt line)",
