      "writtenOn": "2018-12-20T19:17:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If my above understanding is correct, I think the flow is more like:\n\n 1. Master writes a 1 byte register address to the tpm\n 2. Master waits for Cr50 to pulse GPIO_INT_AP_L.\n 3. Cr50 i2c write complete isr fires on the tpm\n   2.1 if exactly 1 byte is received, assume a read transaction is requested, increment i2cs_read_irq_count, and fill tx fifo with requested data.\n   2.2 else, start processing write register request \n 4. Cr50 pulses GPIO_INT_AP_L when data is ready-to-be-read / written\n 5. If master wanted to read, master sends an i2c read command to read data from Cr50 tx fifo.",
